{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Dressing the Part", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Why a Phone Interview?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 13, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Future with Will, Going to and the Present Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use different tenses to talk about the future. Each of them has their own use. It is important to understand the difference between each structure. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about <span class=\"underline\">things that are not decided</span> or when you <span class=\"underline\">make a decision at the moment of speaking</span> for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.<br>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I'll</span> have to prepare better answers for my next interview. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask or talk about <span class=\"underline\">intentions</span>, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>.<br>For example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">I know <span class=\"strong\">I'm going to</span> get nervous and lose control.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are <span class=\"underline\">arranged</span>, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.<br>For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I'm calling</span> her next week to ask for a follow-up. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm going to practice for the interview.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm having an interview tomorrow at 3 p.m.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll call you later so we can practice! ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for information about the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> and <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning/Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Future Continuous</span> <br> <br>  will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future - the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be thinking</span> about what to say all week. </span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will be practicing</span> for the interview this time tomorrow. </span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Future Perfect </span> <br><br> will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk about something that will be complete by a certain time in the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">By the end of the month, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will have had</span> four different interviews. </span> <br> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'ll have answered</span> all the questions by the end of the interview. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to plagiarize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to copy another person's work without giving them credit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For example, once they asked me how I would deal with a journalist whom I suspected was plagiarising.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about job interviews. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "plagiarism", "type": "name"}, {"content": "copying another person's work without giving them credit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You could try to find proof of plagiarism before you say anything.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "straightforward", "type": "name"}, {"content": "clear; easy to follow", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Questions about my experiences or education are fairly straightforward.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "hypothetical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "imaginary; something that could happen in the future", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have a hard time when they describe a hypothetical situation and ask me how I would react.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to suspect", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think; to imagine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For example, once they asked me how I would deal with a journalist whom I suspected was plagiarising. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn9le13ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Think of a hypothetical problem you might have in a workplace.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss what you would do with a partner. Give each other ideas about how to deal with it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the outcome of your discussion with other classmates. Do they have the same opinions?", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I discuss a hypothetical problem with my partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We come up with solutions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the results of the discussion with other people and compare our ideas.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le13ob05re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>:  Hi, Kristi!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>:  Hi, Adam!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>:  How is the job search going?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Oh, it's not easy.  By the end of the month, I will have had four different interviews. Everyone expects me to have a lot of experience. They ask a million questions. I just know I'm going to get nervous and lose control. I'll have to prepare better answers for my next interview.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Can you give me an example of a question you had problems with? That could help me.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I'd love to help. Questions about my experiences or education are fairly straightforward. I have a hard time when they describe a hypothetical situation and ask me how I would react. For example, once they asked me how I would deal with a journalist whom I suspected was plagiarizing. <br>"}, {"image": "engenn9le13ob05re2img06.jpg", "time": "44300", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: What did you say?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I didn't know what to say. Could you help me prepare a good answer?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I can try.  You could try to find proof of plagiarism before you say anything. You can find a lot of things by doing internet searches. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Thanks, that sounds good. Speaking of interviews, how did yours go?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: It was a phone interview!  Can you believe it? All that time I spent worrying about a tie was for nothing.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Why a phone interview?<br>"}, {"image": "engenn9le13ob05re2img07.jpg", "time": "70000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: I don't know. They said I could be invited to meet them for a second interview.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: How did it go?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Not bad, but not great. I'll need to prepare better answers for next time. I'm going to have to decide which articles I'm most proud of. Can you help me?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>:  Sure I can. I'll read your articles again tonight.  <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Adam</span>: Thanks. I'm calling her next week to ask for a follow-up. I'll be thinking about what to say all week.<br>"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le13ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le13ob05re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can make and respond to a request. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "   I can discuss future plans. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about events and experiences related to jobs.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  What advice would you give to a friend about to have a phone interview?  ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What are the top three things you should NOT do in an interview?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feed